  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Humanitarian Response to conflict-affected IDPs, Refugees and Host Communities in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will provide integrated lifesaving assistance in response to the humanitarian needs of the IDPs, host communities, and refugees affected by the continuing armed conflict in Sudan. Development and Peace &#x2013; Caritas Canada, in partnership with CAFOD and NCA, will implement this project through local partners Caritas Sudan and Sahel Sudan SOS in Gedaref, White Nile, and North Darfur. The project will address Protection, WASH (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene), Food Security and Livelihood (MPCA), and Nutrition needs. Protection and GBV services will be integrated with multi-sectoral interventions to comprehensively meet urgent community needs. The project aims to assist 111,618 individuals, with approximately 60% of beneficiaries expected to be women. Participant selection will be conducted in collaboration with OCHA, UNHCR, and relevant authorities to ensure a safe, dignified, and inclusive process.</narrative>
  </description>
